# Environment: DATABASE_URL
# Copy to packages/db/.env for bare Prisma CLI (never commit real secrets).
#
# WARNING: Bare `pnpm --filter @aicaa/db migrate:deploy` and `migrate:status` read
# packages/db/.env. If that file holds a Supabase/production URL, those commands
# target production. For local Docker work, prefer the safe helpers instead:
#
#   pnpm db:docker:up
#   pnpm db:migrate:local
#   pnpm db:migrate:status:local
#
# Local Docker default (see docker-compose.yml — loopback port 5433):
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://prisma:prisma@127.0.0.1:5433/prisma?schema=public"

# Production / staging (operator only — set explicitly when intentionally migrating
# a remote database; do not leave this as the everyday local .env value):
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE?schema=public"
#
# Production migration endpoint (Supabase Shared Pooler, SESSION mode, port 5432).
# Prisma Migrate holds a session-scoped advisory lock for the whole invocation, which the
# transaction-mode endpoint on port 6543 cannot provide. The application runtime keeps using
# transaction mode; only migrations use this form. Placeholder only — never store a real
# credential here, and prefer a process-scoped override over assigning it at all:
#
#   read -rs -p "Migration DATABASE_URL (session pooler, port 5432): " MIGRATE_URL
#   export MIGRATE_URL
#   DATABASE_URL="$MIGRATE_URL" pnpm --filter @aicaa/db migrate:status
#   DATABASE_URL="$MIGRATE_URL" pnpm --filter @aicaa/db migrate:deploy
#   unset MIGRATE_URL
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<PROJECT_REF>:<PASSWORD>@aws-<REGION>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"
#
# DIRECT_URL has no effect in this repository: prisma/schema.prisma declares only
# url = env("DATABASE_URL") and no directUrl, so setting DIRECT_URL changes nothing.

# Capability token pepper/TTL live in apps/web server configuration (CAPABILITY_TOKEN_PEPPER /
# CAPABILITY_TTL_MS). Do not put secrets in this Prisma package env file beyond DATABASE_URL.
